                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7e1bf42f-b18f-422e-b5af-978c84728099",
                        "source_entry_id": "d8058822-c0b5-3e5c-a093-e0980a88aec8",
                        "source_sense_id": "c64b1b4e-ca66-37ff-8d5d-3873a828174a",
                        "target_lang_word": "cello",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cello",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "048681aa-11a9-3ffe-a349-d3e0a8b4943d",
                                        "entry_id": "914e29aa-8348-3cd7-ba73-f5cba9d79f68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large unfretted stringed instrument of the violin family with four strings tuned (lowest to highest) C-G-D-A and an endpin to support its weight, usually played with a bow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de0157a6-4a6b-4057-9713-53c7a8f4665d",
                                                "sense_id": "048681aa-11a9-3ffe-a349-d3e0a8b4943d",
                                                "text": "I haven't always been this cool because I haven't always played guitar. I started out on the cello. Yeah, the cello is a wonderful, beautiful instrument. It's cool to be an adult that plays the cello. Being a kid that played the cello sucked, cause there's no way to be cool when your instrument is larger than you. When you walk to school with a cello you're like a wounded gazelle on the Serengeti, man. The bullies just smell you coming from a mile away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c5e5afe-3b01-4752-9d92-8c3c761c0c5b",
                                                "sense_id": "048681aa-11a9-3ffe-a349-d3e0a8b4943d",
                                                "text": "Fitzgerald saw that Hemingway, oppressed by his mother's influence, was \"still rebelling against having been made to take cello lessons when growing up.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cello",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6b396f3-0c2f-35d5-9807-4143d10dc2a0",
                                        "entry_id": "4ac4fefa-391c-320d-99ab-e4c1c3bad274",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "cellophane"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d21e4432-0b98-467a-8d34-3253b012dbb9",
                                                "sense_id": "b6b396f3-0c2f-35d5-9807-4143d10dc2a0",
                                                "text": "Chocolates arranged in a candy dish or basket, antique or purchased in accordance to^([sic]) the personal taste of the host/hostess, wrapped with cello wrap and tied with a lovely ribbon—decadent!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "21616f6a-378a-4f48-8293-06d025166e6a",
                        "source_entry_id": "d8058822-c0b5-3e5c-a093-e0980a88aec8",
                        "source_sense_id": "c64b1b4e-ca66-37ff-8d5d-3873a828174a",
                        "target_lang_word": "violoncello",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "violoncello",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7aa05789-51b2-39a3-8672-39be0f8efc2a",
                                        "entry_id": "0196a7c7-9063-3500-aaba-6e7815eafa90",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of cello."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12afc9a6-fce7-4687-946e-5cbcd437a141",
                                                "sense_id": "7aa05789-51b2-39a3-8672-39be0f8efc2a",
                                                "text": "A tentative violoncello is playing, invisible and plaintive, then stops with an asthmatic scrape of catgut."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fc4a962-0729-4381-9cc0-401f62145573",
                                                "sense_id": "7aa05789-51b2-39a3-8672-39be0f8efc2a",
                                                "text": "Preserved under the rock-hard amber varnish was a beautifully crafted mythological scene depicting a nude man in a lush landscape playing a violoncello to a rapt audience of peaceful animals, including a jaguar, lion, swan, fox, peacock, horse, parrot, dogs, badger, deer, bull, ostrich, and no less than an elephant coming over the hill to join them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a11478a3-fdbf-4a08-9494-98a1d3f3d138",
                        "source_entry_id": "d8058822-c0b5-3e5c-a093-e0980a88aec8",
                        "source_sense_id": "c64b1b4e-ca66-37ff-8d5d-3873a828174a",
